<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE task PUBLIC "-//OASIS//DTD DITA Task//EN" "task.dtd">
<task id="data-api-token">
  <title>Create an account with an API token</title>
  <taskbody>
    <data name="doc-detective" value='test {"testId":"data-api-token","if":"$$platform oneOf [linux, mac, windows]","publicVariables":["ACCOUNT_*"],"detectSteps":true}'/>
    <context>
      <p>Keep the API address and your token in a <codeph>.env</codeph> file next to this page:</p>
      <codeblock outputclass="language-text">API_URL=http://localhost:8092/api
API_TOKEN=your-api-token</codeblock>
    </context>
    <steps>
      <step><cmd>Load the variables from your <codeph>.env</codeph> file.</cmd>
        <info><data name="doc-detective" value='step {"loadVariables":".env"}'/></info></step>
      <step><cmd>Send a <codeph>POST</codeph> request to <codeph>$API_URL/accounts</codeph> with the header <codeph>Authorization: Bearer $API_TOKEN</codeph> and this body:</cmd>
        <info><codeblock outputclass="language-json">{"name": "Wren", "plan": "team", "seats": 5, "roles": ["admin", "billing"]}</codeblock>
          <p>The API returns status <codeph>200</codeph> and the new account, with <codeph>plan</codeph> set to <codeph>team</codeph>. Note the account's <codeph>name</codeph>, its <codeph>seats</codeph>, and its first role.</p>
          <data name="doc-detective" value='step {"httpRequest":{"url":"$API_URL/accounts","method":"post","request":{"headers":{"Authorization":"Bearer $API_TOKEN"},"body":{"name":"Wren","plan":"team","seats":5,"roles":["admin","billing"]}},"response":{"body":{"name":"Wren"}}},"assertions":["$$outputs.response.statusCode == 200","$$outputs.response.body.plan == \"team\""],"variables":{"ACCOUNT_NAME":"$$response.body.name","ACCOUNT_SEATS":"jq($$response.body, \".seats\")","ACCOUNT_ROLE":"$$response.body.roles[0]"}}'/></info></step>
      <step><cmd>Look up the account. Send a <codeph>GET</codeph> request to <codeph>$API_URL/accounts?name=&lt;name&gt;&amp;seats=&lt;seats&gt;&amp;role=&lt;role&gt;</codeph>. The response shows the same name, seat count, and role.</cmd>
        <info><data name="doc-detective" value='step {"httpRequest":{"url":"$API_URL/accounts?name=$ACCOUNT_NAME&amp;seats=$ACCOUNT_SEATS&amp;role=$ACCOUNT_ROLE","method":"get","response":{"body":{"name":"Wren","seats":"5","role":"admin"}}},"assertions":"$$outputs.response.body.seats == $ACCOUNT_SEATS"}'/></info></step>
    </steps>
    <data name="doc-detective" value="test end"/>
  </taskbody>
</task>
